From ca5c0932339205a371b66f789cf026eb7ba40ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:13:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mediacodec: AV1 with the hardware decoder (video/av01)
Message-Id: <20261110-dvfel-mediacodec-av1@djnice>

VLC 3's MediaCodec module had no AV1: an AV1 film was decoded by dav1d on
the CPU, which cannot keep up with 4K on these boxes (the pictures came
later and later, 85 s behind after two minutes, and all were dropped: no
picture at all, the sound on), and with no hardware decoder the firmware's
frame rate switch was not made either. The Amlogic boxes have
OMX.amlogic.av1.decoder.awesome2 (video/av01, up to 8192x4320); its csd-0
is the AV1CodecConfigurationRecord, the av1C the container gives VLC.
---
 modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
index b822a6bc9f..a1be8d13b6 100644
--- a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
@@ -1221,6 +1221,9 @@ static int OpenDecoder(vlc_object_t *p_this, pf_MediaCodecApi_init pf_init)
         case VLC_CODEC_VC1:  mime = "video/wvc1"; break;
         case VLC_CODEC_VP8:  mime = "video/x-vnd.on2.vp8"; break;
         case VLC_CODEC_VP9:  mime = "video/x-vnd.on2.vp9"; break;
+        /* AV1: csd-0 the AV1CodecConfigurationRecord (av1C, the container's
+         * codec private data), as Android's own extractors give it */
+        case VLC_CODEC_AV1:  mime = "video/av01"; break;
         }
     }
     else
